# Implementation Plan: In-Store Discovery & Local Retail (O2O) - Phase 1

Convert **shopMe** into an Online-to-Offline (O2O) physical retail platform where customers discover nearby local shops, check in-store products & availability, navigate via Google Maps, contact shopkeepers via WhatsApp/Call, and visit the physical store to purchase.

---

## Phase 1 Objectives (Best Starting Foundation)

Before building reservations or in-store hold features, the foundation of physical store discovery must be in place:
1. **Geo-Location & Near-Me Search**: Store Latitude/Longitude and calculate real-time distance in KM (`distance_km`) using the Haversine formula in PostgreSQL.
2. **City & Pincode Filter**: Allow users to filter shops by city/pincode or search radius.
3. **Direct In-Store Contact**: Add WhatsApp number and auto-generate WhatsApp inquiry links & Google Maps direction URLs.
4. **Shop Counter QR Code**: An endpoint (`GET /shops/{slug}/qr` & `GET /shops/me/qr`) that generates a downloadable/scannable QR code for the shopkeeper's billing counter.

---

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> **Cart & Payment tables in DB**: 
> Previously created migrations for `carts`, `orders`, `payments` can remain untouched or be archived, since we are pivoting from e-commerce delivery to in-store visits. The next phase will introduce an **In-Store Reservation / Item Hold** module instead of online checkout.

> [!TIP]
> **Haversine Distance Query**: 
> We will use the standard earth radius formula (6371 km) in PostgreSQL SQL query. This requires no external GIS plugins (works natively on standard PostgreSQL without needing PostGIS extensions).

